        "name": "Gerrit AI review for Lustre",
        "display_name": "AI review",
        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-10-17 05:31:25.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. The new output parses as YAML for every multi-line nodemap value (idmap, ranges, offset, fileset, exports, enable_cap_mask). There are optional notes inline that can wait until the patch is next refreshed.\n\nOne gap in coverage: sanity-sec test_25c never makes a block-mapping value, so it passes with or without this fix. Only nodemap.*.enable_cap_mask prints a block mapping (\"type: ...\\ncaps: ...\"), and only when the cap type is not \"off\". test_25c leaves it at the default \"off\", which prints one line. If test_25c ran something like `$LCTL nodemap_set_cap --name $nm --type mask --caps cap_chown` before the get_param, it would catch this bug, and it would also make the Test-Parameters run worth something.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
