          "date": "2026-10-17 07:23:32.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-18502 utils: indent a multi-line value for get_param -y",
        "message": "LU-18502 utils: indent a multi-line value for get_param -y\n\nWith --yaml, \"lctl get_param\" prints the first line of a multi-line\nvalue on the line of the parameter name. When the value is a block\nmapping, a YAML parser rejects the output. A block mapping cannot\nstart on the line of its key. For example, nodemap.*.enable_cap_mask\nwith a cap type other than \"off\" prints \"type: ...\" and \"caps: ...\"\non two lines.\n\nIn print_param_internal(), start a multi-line value on the next line.\nIndent each line of the value by two spaces. A parser then reads the\nlines as the value of the parameter name.\n\nFixes: 5768bf35fd (\"LU-18502 utils: Support YAML for get_param parameter names\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-sec env=ONLY=25c\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5\nChange-Id: I582ee0634a8af5b71eb86d39b64f930b4df47730\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
